final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_54jar")
province = 71
blurb = "Depicts two red-crowned cranes, one about to land, in a marsh.

The title of the print lists three villages northwest of the Yoshiwara pleasure quarters. The viewer is looking from Minowa and Kanasugi toward Mikawashima, to the west or northwest.

Mikawashima was where the shōgun's Crane Hunt occurred almost every year during the winter months, when cranes migrated to Japan. Aside from the one or two birds taken on each hunt, the cranes of Mikawashima were carefully protected. The figure in the background is carrying buckets filled with rice to feed them.

The crane's feathers feature karazuri (\"empty printing\"), or \"gauffrage\", a technique of embossing paper by pressing a block into the paper without ink."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
